# Line endings are pinned, not negotiated.
#
# Without this file git honours each machine's `core.autocrlf`, which on Windows is `true`.
# Every source file here is authored LF, prettier writes LF, and the engine ships to macOS
# and Linux as well — so a Windows checkout that silently becomes CRLF turns the first
# cross-platform commit into a whole-repo diff. `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf on every
# platform: LF in the repository and LF in the working copy, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched. `text=auto` guesses from content and usually guesses
# right, but an icon that gets newline-translated is a corrupt icon, and the failure shows
# up as an unsignable app rather than as a diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.node binary

# Generated, and enormous. Marking it means `git diff` stays readable and GitHub does not
# count 40k lines of resolved dependencies as authored code in the language stats.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true

# Salvaged research dumps: prose, not source. Excluding them from language detection stops
# GitHub from reporting this repository as majority Markdown.
research/raw/** linguist-documentation=true
